Remove combine.c's PLUS->IOR conversion from GCC 2.7.2's simplify_rtx.

This is THE patch that defines the Bushido Blade 2 oracle compiler. It is
applied by tools/build_oracle_cc1.sh to a pristine checkout of
decompals/mips-gcc-2.7.2 @ 43d1cdb67ed135879869b5266f01efaaada5e35a inside a
scratch tree; tools/gcc-2.7.2/ is gitignored, which is why the patch lives
here, tracked, instead of as an edit in the compiler tree.

WHAT IT DOES
  Stock GCC rewrites `a + b` into `a | b` whenever it can prove the two
  operands have no bits in common (`nonzero_bits(a) & nonzero_bits(b) == 0`).
  Removing the conversion makes the compiler emit `addu`/`addiu` where stock
  emits `or`/`ori`. Behaviourally that is the ONLY difference: a cc1 built
  with this patch is byte-identical in output to the frozen 2026-05-18 oracle
  binary (sha1 045c9543d39ab8109583b92137c7adde084f7a25) on all 32 project
  TUs, and `simplify_rtx` matches its shipped size exactly (0x39ab vs stock
  0x3a11).

WHY IT IS HERE (owner election, docs/grind/decisions.md 2026-08-07, d99ab6a6)
  The patch was introduced accidentally: a 2026-05-18 compiler-patch
  experiment whose output binary became the project compiler and was never
  reverted. It is retained — now visible, pinned and reproducible — on the
  SOTN pattern: that project's cc1-psx-26 is likewise a PATCHED GCC built
  from a pinned upstream commit and distributed as a hash-verified binary.
  The community bar is "visible, pinned, reproducible", not "unpatched
  stock". Retention is MATCH-PROVEN (full-build SHA1 == the original
  executable), and is NOT a claim that the original PsyQ compiler behaved
  this way — that question is recorded OPEN in docs/ORACLE-COMPILER.md, with
  evidence pointing both ways.

  This does not loosen the no-compiler-divergence rule. That freeze stands
  for everything else; this single documented, owner-elected, match-proven
  patch is its only in-scope amendment.

diff --git a/combine.c b/combine.c
index 473adc8..fbb05c8 100644
--- a/combine.c
+++ b/combine.c
@@ -3615,15 +3615,6 @@ simplify_rtx (x, op0_mode, last, in_dest)
 				 GET_MODE_BITSIZE (mode) - 1),
 	   GET_MODE_BITSIZE (mode) - 1);
 
-      /* If we are adding two things that have no bits in common, convert
-	 the addition into an IOR.  This will often be further simplified,
-	 for example in cases like ((a & 1) + (a & 2)), which can
-	 become a & 3.  */
-
-      if (GET_MODE_BITSIZE (mode) <= HOST_BITS_PER_WIDE_INT
-	  && (nonzero_bits (XEXP (x, 0), mode)
-	      & nonzero_bits (XEXP (x, 1), mode)) == 0)
-	return gen_binary (IOR, mode, XEXP (x, 0), XEXP (x, 1));
       break;
 
     case MINUS:
